       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. TCCSFTP.
       AUTHOR.     JEFF BUNGO
       INSTALLATION.  GOODYEAR TIRE & RUBBER CO.
       DATE-WRITTEN.   09/18/97.
      *************************************************************
      *  THIS PROGRAM IS USED TO LOAD FTP INFO TO EXECUTE IBM     *
      *  FTP COMMANDS IN BATCH MODE.                              *
      *                                                           *
      *  THE FOLLOWING INFORMATION IS LOADED INTO A QTXTSRC       *
      *  BATCH MEMBER:                                            *
      *      RECORD 1 - USER ID AND PASSWORD                      *
      *        "    2 - FTP COMMAND                               *
      *        "    3 - FTP COMMAND             (IF NEEDED)       *
      *        "    4 - FTP COMMAND             (IF NEEDED)       *
      *        "    5 - FTP COMMAND             (IF NEEDED)       *
      *        "    6 - FTP COMMAND             (IF NEEDED)       *
      *        "    7 - FTP QUIT COMMAND                          *
      *                                                           *
      *  THE RESULTS SHOULD RESEMBLE THE FOLLOWING:               *
      *      ccs    ccs                                           *
      *      ascii                                                *
      *      put qtemp/ccsdata.ccsdata /apps/ccs/data/ccsdata.jddd*
      *      quit                                                 *
      *                                                           *
      *************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-AS400.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.   REQUESTOR IS WORK-STATION
                        SYSTEM-CONSOLE IS CONSOLE
                        SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN IS SHUTDOWN-SWITCH
                               ON STATUS IS SYSTEM-SHUTDOWN-REQUESTED
                        LOCAL-DATA IS LOCAL-DATA-AREA.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
            SELECT QTXTSRC-FILE ASSIGN TO DATABASE-QTXTSRC
                   ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                   ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
                   RECORD KEY IS SRCSEQ
                   FILE STATUS IS QTXTSRC-SK.
       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  QTXTSRC-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  QTXTSRC-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF QTXTSRC.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       77  CCTR                                PIC 9(3).
       77  TCTR                                PIC 9(3).
       01  FILE-STATUS-KEYS.
           03  QTXTSRC-SK                      PIC X(2)  VALUE ZERO.

       01  JUL-DDD                             PIC X(3).
       01  DATE-CYMD.
           05  DATE-YYYY.
               10  DATE-CC                     PIC X(2).
               10  DATE-YY                     PIC X(2).
           05  DATE-MM                         PIC X(2).
           05  DATE-DD                         PIC X(2).
       01  DATE2 REDEFINES DATE-CYMD.
           05  DATE2-CC                        PIC X(2).
           05  DATE-YMD                        PIC X(6).

       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01  USER                                PIC X(10).
       01  PWD                                 PIC X(10).
       01  FFILE                               PIC X(32).
       01  TFILE                               PIC X(50).
       01  TTYPE                               PIC X(10).

       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING USER PWD FFILE TFILE TTYPE.
       000-OPEN.
           OPEN OUTPUT QTXTSRC-FILE.
       010-MAIN.
           PERFORM 100-PROCESS                 THRU 100-EXIT.
           PERFORM 900-CLOSE-FILES             THRU 900-EXIT.
       010-EOJ.
           GOBACK.

       100-PROCESS.
           PERFORM 110-LOAD-ID                 THRU 110-EXIT.
           PERFORM 120-TRANSFER-TYPE           THRU 120-EXIT.
           PERFORM 130-PUT-INFO                THRU 130-EXIT.
           PERFORM 190-LOAD-QUIT               THRU 190-EXIT.
       100-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       110-LOAD-ID.
           MOVE 10                           TO SRCSEQ.
           MOVE ZEROES                       TO SRCDAT.
           MOVE SPACES                       TO SRCDTA.
           MOVE USER                         TO SRCDTA (1:10).
           MOVE PWD                          TO SRCDTA (12:10).
           PERFORM WRITE-QTXTSRC.
       110-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       120-TRANSFER-TYPE.
           MOVE 20                           TO SRCSEQ.
           MOVE ZEROES                       TO SRCDAT.
           MOVE SPACES                       TO SRCDTA.
           MOVE TTYPE                        TO SRCDTA (1:10).
           PERFORM WRITE-QTXTSRC.
       120-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       130-PUT-INFO.
      *
      *    FORMAT OF FTP PUT STATEMENT
      *
      *    PUT MYLIB/MYFILE.MYMBR  unix1/unix2/unix3.jddd
      *
           MOVE 1                            TO CCTR.
           MOVE 30                           TO SRCSEQ.
           MOVE ZEROES                       TO SRCDAT.
           MOVE SPACES                       TO SRCDTA.
           MOVE "PUT"                        TO SRCDTA (CCTR:3).

           COMPUTE CCTR = CCTR + 3 + 1.
           MOVE 0 TO TCTR.
           INSPECT FFILE TALLYING TCTR
               FOR CHARACTERS BEFORE INITIAL " ".
           MOVE FFILE                        TO SRCDTA (CCTR:TCTR).

           COMPUTE CCTR = CCTR + TCTR + 1.
           MOVE 0 TO TCTR.
           INSPECT TFILE TALLYING TCTR
               FOR CHARACTERS BEFORE INITIAL " ".
           MOVE TFILE                        TO SRCDTA (CCTR:TCTR).

           COMPUTE CCTR = CCTR + TCTR.
           MOVE ".j"                         TO SRCDTA(CCTR:2).

           COMPUTE CCTR = CCTR + 2.
           ACCEPT DATE-YMD FROM DATE.
           IF DATE-YY > 70
               MOVE "19" TO DATE-CC
           ELSE
               MOVE "20" TO DATE-CC.
           CALL "CJULIAN" USING DATE-YYYY DATE-MM DATE-DD JUL-DDD.
           MOVE JUL-DDD                      TO SRCDTA(CCTR:3).

           PERFORM WRITE-QTXTSRC.
       130-EXIT.
           EXIT.


       190-LOAD-QUIT.
           MOVE 9999                         TO SRCSEQ.
           MOVE ZEROES                       TO SRCDAT.
           MOVE SPACES                       TO SRCDTA.
           MOVE "QUIT"                       TO SRCDTA (1:4).
           PERFORM WRITE-QTXTSRC.
       190-EXIT.
           EXIT.

       WRITE-QTXTSRC.
           WRITE QTXTSRC-REC.
           IF QTXTSRC-SK NOT EQUAL ZERO
               THEN
                   DISPLAY "TCCSFTP WRITE ERROR: " QTXTSRC-SK, " ",
                    SRCDTA.

       900-CLOSE-FILES.
           CLOSE QTXTSRC-FILE.
       900-EXIT.
           EXIT.
